course: dictionary
lesson: 8748
title: A session is a set period of time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A session is a set period of time spent doing one activity, such as a lesson, a practice or a meeting. «Ten minutes every day builds a skill faster than one long session a week.» Here a session is one block of time spent learning, and the word long tells you it lasted a while.
explain: Look at the words around session to find its meaning. «A training session» and «a homework session» are times spent training or doing homework. «Fitness builds from many small, regular sessions» tells you that sessions can be short or long. Ask: what could I put in place of session? Try «a block of time for practice» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Session has other meanings too. A parliament or court holds a session when it meets, and «in session» means it is meeting right now. Part of the school day, like a morning session, is also a session. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right.
fact: A session is a set period of time spent doing one activity.
fact: «Training session» means a set time spent practising a sport or a skill.
fact: «In session» means a parliament or court is meeting right now.
fact: «Skills grow with practice: ten minutes every day builds a skill much faster than one long session a week.» Short, regular practice often works better than one long session.
fact: On a computer, a session is the time you are logged in, so log out at the end.
exercise: «Ten minutes every day builds a skill faster than one long session a week.» What does session mean here? | *A period of time spent doing one activity | A small piece of paper | A quiet room for reading | A type of football boot
exercise: «The court is in session, so the judge is listening.» What does in session mean? | Closed for the day | Lost and missing | *Meeting right now | Finished for ever
exercise: Ben's «homework session» took an hour. What is a homework session? | A homework book | A bag for school books | A teacher who sets homework | *A period of time spent doing homework
test: «The rules are short: kit out of the bag and washed after every session.» What is a session in this sentence? | A rule about showers | *A period of time spent doing an activity, such as training | A kind of towel | A bag for kit
test: Ava says, «Fitness builds from many small, regular sessions, not from one huge session.» What does the word huge tell you about the session? | It was a tiny, quick activity | *It was a very large amount of time spent on one activity | It was a meeting in a court | It was a computer login
exam: Which sentence uses session to mean a meeting of a parliament? | «Learning an instrument is like building a wall brick by brick.» | «Tell an adult about any new rash or sore.» | *«The parliament holds its next session on Monday.» | «Short daily practice builds a skill faster.»
